  <body>
    <front><contents /></front>
    <chapter>
      <heading>
        Software documentation for the TTIORunSelection class
      </heading>
      <class name="TTIORunSelection" super="NSObject">
        <declared>TTIORunSelection.h</declared>
        <desc>
          <em>Description forthcoming.</em>
        </desc>
        <method type="TTIOAcquisitionRun*" factory="yes">
          <sel>analyticalRunIn:</sel>
          <arg type="TTIOSpectralDataset*">ds</arg>
          <sel>layer:</sel>
          <arg type="NSString*">layer</arg>
          <sel>error:</sel>
          <arg type="NSError**">error</arg>
          <desc>
            Select an analytical run (any spectrum class — MS or
            NMR) by <code><var>layer</var></code> name, or the
            single run when unambiguous. Mirrors Python's
            <code>analytical_run</code>. @param <var>ds</var>
            The opened dataset to select from. @param
            <var>layer</var> Optional run name; <code>nil</code>
            /empty selects the sole run when unambiguous. @param
            <var>error</var> On failure, set to an
            <code>NSError</code> whose
            <code>localizedDescription</code> mirrors Python's
            <code>KeyError</code> text. @return The selected
            run, or <code>nil</code> +
            <code><var>error</var></code> when there are no
            analytical runs, the named
            <code><var>layer</var></code> is absent, or
            <code><var>layer</var></code> is <code>nil</code>
            and multiple runs are present (ambiguous).
          </desc>
        </method>
        <method type="TTIOGenomicRun*" factory="yes">
          <sel>genomicRunIn:</sel>
          <arg type="TTIOSpectralDataset*">ds</arg>
          <sel>layer:</sel>
          <arg type="NSString*">layer</arg>
          <sel>error:</sel>
          <arg type="NSError**">error</arg>
          <desc>
            Select a genomic run by
            <code><var>layer</var></code> name, or the single
            run when unambiguous. Mirrors Python's
            <code>genomic_run</code>.
            <p>
              Returns the dataset's read-side
              <code>TTIOGenomicRun</code>; callers needing a
              write-side run for BAM/CRAM export pass the
              result through
              <code>
                <ref type="method" id="+writtenFromGenomicRun:">
                  +writtenFromGenomicRun:
                </ref>
              </code>
              .
            </p>
            @param <var>ds</var> The opened dataset to select
            from. @param <var>layer</var> Optional genomic-run
            name; <code>nil</code> /empty selects the sole run.
            @param <var>error</var> On failure, set to an
            <code>NSError</code> mirroring Python's
            <code>KeyError</code> text. @return The selected
            genomic run, or <code>nil</code> +
            <code><var>error</var></code>.
          </desc>
        </method>
        <method type="TTIOAcquisitionRun*" factory="yes">
          <sel>nmrRunIn:</sel>
          <arg type="TTIOSpectralDataset*">ds</arg>
          <sel>layer:</sel>
          <arg type="NSString*">layer</arg>
          <sel>error:</sel>
          <arg type="NSError**">error</arg>
          <desc>
            Select an NMR run, preferring the NMR-classed run,
            falling back to the sole analytical run. Mirrors
            Python's <code>nmr_run</code>. @param
            <var>ds</var> The opened dataset to select from.
            @param <var>layer</var> Optional run name;
            <code>nil</code> /empty prefers the NMR-classed run,
            else the sole run. @param <var>error</var> On failure,
            set to an <code>NSError</code> mirroring Python's
            <code>KeyError</code> text. @return The selected
            run, or <code>nil</code> +
            <code><var>error</var></code>.
          </desc>
        </method>
        <method type="TTIOWrittenGenomicRun*" factory="yes">
          <sel>writtenFromGenomicRun:</sel>
          <arg type="TTIOGenomicRun*">readSideRun</arg>
          <desc>
            Materialise a read-side
            <code>TTIOGenomicRun</code> (as returned by the
            opened dataset's <code>genomicRuns</code>) into a
            write-side <code>TTIOWrittenGenomicRun</code>
            for BAM / CRAM export, whose
            <code>
              <ref type="method" id="-writeRun:">
                -writeRun:
              </ref>
            </code>
            requires the written form.
            <p>
              ObjC port of the Java
              <code>RunSelection.toWritten</code> shared
              conversion: every per-read field is
              materialised from the run's index and its
              per-read <code>TTIOAlignedRead</code> objects
              into the parallel <code>NSData</code> /
              <code>NSArray</code> channels the writer expects.
              Sequences and qualities are concatenated and
              sliced by the offsets/lengths channels.
              Compression defaults to
              <code>TTIOCompressionNone</code>.
            </p>
            @param <var>readSideRun</var> A read-side
            <code>TTIOGenomicRun</code>. @return A freshly
            materialised
            <code>TTIOWrittenGenomicRun</code>.
          </desc>
        </method>
      </class>
    </chapter>
  </body>
</gsdoc>
